============================================================================
A  IS THE BRAIN-AGE GAP THE WRONG ONE NUMBER?
============================================================================
  Both arms are ONE number per subject, plus age. The only difference
  is which linear combination of the same information it is.

  AD vs CN   one PCA component minus brain-age gap: +0.024
             95% CI [+0.016, +0.032]  p=0.000  -> REAL
  MCI vs CN  one PCA component minus brain-age gap: +0.005
             95% CI [-0.002, +0.014]  p=0.196  -> not distinguishable

  the single component, region by region (its loadings):
    کل مغز           +0.451
    هیپوکامپ         +0.450
    گیجگاهی میانی    +0.431
    دوکی             +0.425
    آنتورینال        +0.396
    بطن‌ها           -0.268
    variance explained: 58%

============================================================================
B  IS THE COUPLING RESULT A VARIANCE ARTEFACT?  (Spearman = rank based)
============================================================================
  Pearson   observed 0.119   null 0.046 [0.026, 0.073]   p=0.0000
  Spearman  observed 0.124   null 0.043 [0.024, 0.074]   p=0.0000

  variance of the deviations by group (the thing that could confound):
    CN         mean SD across regions = 0.98
    MCI        mean SD across regions = 1.17
    Dementia   mean SD across regions = 1.25

